    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x0a5bsx",
      "content": "1. Who is known as the 'Father of Goan Nationalism'?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pia1xaq",
      "content": "   (a) Ram Manohar Lohia   (b) Tristao de Braganza Cunha   (c) Abbé Faria   (d) Manohar Parrikar"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "52trjfm",
      "content": "<strong>   Answer: (b) Tristao de Braganza Cunha</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "v3pqdml",
      "content": "2. On which date was Goa liberated from Portuguese rule?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jwc3s2r",
      "content": "   (a) August 15, 1947   (b) January 26, 1950   (c) December 19, 1961   (d) May 30, 1987"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "yo28uwp",
      "content": "<strong>   Answer: (c) December 19, 1961</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0l1a1qd",
      "content": "3. The oldest and best-preserved temple in Goa, built during the Kadamba period, is located at:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qc6s929",
      "content": "   (a) Mardol   (b) Tambdi Surla   (c) Kavlem   (d) Bandode"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t29emzs",
      "content": "<strong>   Answer: (b) Tambdi Surla — Shri Mahadeva Temple (12th Century)</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4pn7n24",
      "content": "4. Alfonso de Albuquerque conquered Goa in which year?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6uwdvi4",
      "content": "   (a) 1498   (b) 1510   (c) 1542   (d) 1560"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "xs8bdip",
      "content": "<strong>   Answer: (b) 1510</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "q4vvm3c",
      "content": "5. The Goa Inquisition was established in:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uotfnpt",
      "content": "   (a) 1510   (b) 1542   (c) 1560   (d) 1612"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "lq928fr",
      "content": "<strong>   Answer: (c) 1560</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "aytv56l",
      "content": "6. Operation Vijay was launched for the liberation of Goa. Who was the Prime Minister of India at that time?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wmozxm3",
      "content": "   (a) Indira Gandhi   (b) Jawaharlal Nehru   (c) Lal Bahadur Shastri   (d) Sardar Patel"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "gw0aikv",
      "content": "<strong>   Answer: (b) Jawaharlal Nehru</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kt9bm6p",
      "content": "7. The 'Opinion Poll' in Goa was held in which year?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a2ewa8t",
      "content": "   (a) 1961   (b) 1963   (c) 1967   (d) 1987"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qnns8z0",
      "content": "<strong>   Answer: (c) 1967 (January 16, 1967)</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fnjr9sh",
      "content": "8. Goa was granted statehood under which Constitutional Amendment?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g6h2y1x",
      "content": "   (a) 52nd   (b) 56th   (c) 71st   (d) 73rd"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ea9m0hw",
      "content": "<strong>   Answer: (b) 56th Constitutional Amendment Act, 1987</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6241o39",
      "content": "9. Who was the first Chief Minister of Goa?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "82itk4l",
      "content": "   (a) Shashikala Kakodkar   (b) Pratapsinh Rane   (c) Dayanand Bandodkar   (d) Manohar Parrikar"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "4kc2gah",
      "content": "<strong>   Answer: (c) Dayanand Bandodkar</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5ido0xe",
      "content": "10. The Usgalimal petroglyphs are located on the banks of which river?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x04ubda",
      "content": "   (a) Mandovi   (b) Zuari   (c) Kushavati   (d) Sal"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "CHAPTER 9: PRACTICE QUESTIONS (GOA PSC / SI LEVEL)",
      "id": "fddz029"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cq5otjl",
      "content": "<strong>   Answer: (c) Kushavati River, Sanguem Taluka</strong>"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5s0d1i",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9.2 Geography — MCQs"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "glx1klr",
      "content": "11. What is the highest peak in Goa?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0j9jwpu",
      "content": "   (a) Dudhasagar   (b) Sonsogor   (c) Tamhini   (d) Chorla"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "27bdmu0",
      "content": "<strong>   Answer: (b) Sonsogor (1,166 m), Sanguem Taluka</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h7rkmdn",
      "content": "12. Goa's only National Park is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g14r7sj",
      "content": "   (a) Cotigao Wildlife Sanctuary   (b) Bondla Wildlife Sanctuary   (c) Bhagwan Mahavir National Park   (d) Netravali Wildlife Sanctuary"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bkzr01d",
      "content": "<strong>   Answer: (c) Bhagwan Mahavir National Park (Mollem, Sanguem)</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "asejfc6",
      "content": "13. Which beach in Goa is known as the 'Queen of Beaches'?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hjqf3ln",
      "content": "   (a) Palolem   (b) Baga   (c) Calangute   (d) Colva"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "xys68ww",
      "content": "<strong>   Answer: (c) Calangute</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yfcqq45",
      "content": "14. Mormugao Port is located at the mouth of which river?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1wkvuop",
      "content": "   (a) Mandovi   (b) Sal   (c) Zuari   (d) Betul"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "w57ocrq",
      "content": "<strong>   Answer: (c) Zuari River</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zcykjbf",
      "content": "15. Goa's newest taluka created in 2015 is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wnrcfni",
      "content": "   (a) Quepem   (b) Canacona   (c) Dharbandora   (d) Pernem"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "m55n4yj",
      "content": "<strong>   Answer: (c) Dharbandora</strong>"
    },
    {
      "id": "9p9jdan",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9.3 Culture, Art & Heritage — MCQs"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c2gbd1g",
      "content": "16. The Churches and Convents of Old Goa were inscribed as UNESCO World Heritage Site in:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l88wttp",
      "content": "   (a) 1982   (b) 1986   (c) 1992   (d) 2000"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "9302396",
      "content": "<strong>   Answer: (b) 1986</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yzt1xk6",
      "content": "17. Bebinca is known as:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bxvajbw",
      "content": "   (a) State Drink of Goa   (b) Queen of Goan Desserts   (c) State Fish of Goa   (d) A folk dance"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vwxkadx",
      "content": "<strong>   Answer: (b) Queen of Goan Desserts</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w1pka09",
      "content": "18. Who was awarded the Jnanpith Award 2022 from Goa?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "56phjnn",
      "content": "   (a) Ravindra Kelekar   (b) Pundalik Naik   (c) Damodar Mauzo   (d) BB Borkar"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vvsbdqo",
      "content": "<strong>   Answer: (c) Damodar Mauzo (Konkani writer)</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qabacmn",
      "content": "19. Konkani was added to the 8th Schedule of the Constitution by which Amendment?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "v9qkttj",
      "content": "   (a) 56th   (b) 71st   (c) 73rd   (d) 86th"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hu2iyav",
      "content": "<strong>   Answer: (b) 71st Constitutional Amendment, 1992</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2fyfb1z",
      "content": "20. The state animal of Goa is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4b3vtax",
      "content": "   (a) Leopard   (b) Indian Elephant   (c) Gaur (Indian Bison)   (d) Sloth Bear"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ngs0ro6",
      "content": "<strong>   Answer: (c) Gaur (Indian Bison) — Bos gaurus</strong>"
    },
    {
      "id": "m30epx1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9.4 Economy and Governance — MCQs"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dmxiog5",
      "content": "21. Goa has the highest _______ among all Indian states:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8k18m37",
      "content": "   (a) Literacy rate   (b) Per capita income   (c) Forest cover percentage   (d) Coastline"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Goa PSC and SI exams emphasize state-specific history, geography, and heritage questions.",
        "Economy and Governance sections frequently test knowledge of key policies and administrative frameworks.",
        "Consistently solving topic-wise MCQs improves retention and time management during the actual examination."
      ],
      "id": "1midn42"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "7kguk1w",
      "content": "<strong>   Answer: (b) Per Capita Income</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "so0pa8m",
      "content": "22. Feni, Goa's heritage drink, has been given which tag?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wiis7d6",
      "content": "   (a) Heritage Tag   (b) GI (Geographical Indication) Tag   (c) Organic Certification   (d) UNESCO Intangible Heritage"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jh2c3h7",
      "content": "<strong>   Answer: (b) Geographical Indication (GI) Tag</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l5g8mpn",
      "content": "23. Goa is unique in India as the only state with:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bkwdnkq",
      "content": "   (a) No SC Reservation   (b) A Uniform Civil Code (UCC)   (c) No Lok Sabha seats   (d) Only 1 district"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0ychrau",
      "content": "<strong>   Answer: (b) A Uniform Civil Code — based on the Portuguese Civil Code</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8tg1wht",
      "content": "24. The Manohar International Airport (Mopa Airport) was inaugurated in:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2fr43q2",
      "content": "   (a) 2019   (b) 2021   (c) 2022   (d) 2023"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hsv5u2a",
      "content": "<strong>   Answer: (d) January 2023 (inaugurated by PM Narendra Modi)</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ytevvab",
      "content": "25. Konkan Railway passes through Goa. The major railway junction in South Goa is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vbpmvl1",
      "content": "   (a) Thivim   (b) Karmali   (c) Madgaon (Margao)   (d) Vasco"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "nndfdku",
      "content": "<strong>   Answer: (c) Madgaon (Margao) Junction</strong>"
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}